{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally on the Aegean Sea", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Desert", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Out and About in the City > Istanbul", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Ask and Say Where Places Are", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you ask where things are, you use polite questions. When you say where things are, you often use prepositions of place.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking Where Things Are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Saying Where Things Are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is between ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'd like to know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They are below ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you know where ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is in ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where is ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They are at ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Where is the Middle East? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's an area in Western Asia and Egypt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They go from one place to another.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item. <br>You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns. <br><br>You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some people think the desert is an <span class=\"underline\">endless</span> desert of rolling dunes. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There's still <span class=\"underline\">a lot of </span>sand in the desert.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">More and more</span> nomads traded their wandering life for an urban one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"less/fewer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a smaller number/amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"no/none\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"any/not any\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ask about a number or amount/say there is no\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"some\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a small number/amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a lot of/lots of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a very large number/amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more than you need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"as much as you need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"endless\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never ending\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "desert", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large area of land covered in sand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They crossed the desert on a camel.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about the desert.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "camel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large animal, used to travel in the desert ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sit on the camel and travel across the desert.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nomad", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who moves from one place to another", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nomads never live in the same spot for long.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "shade", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where the direct sunlight is blocked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I find it cooler in the shade on a hot summer day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "tent ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a moveable shelter, made of cloth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I sleep in my tent when I am camping.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rural", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area away from the city", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Living in rural areas is more peaceful and relaxed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "urban", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a city or town", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is noisier and busier in an urban area.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "wandering ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "moving from place to place without direction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nomads are wandering people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Do some research on an  animal that does useful work for humans (not a camel).  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Name the animal and say where it lives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5-7 sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe the animal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what it does and what it is used for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write 50-75 words about a work animal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say where it lives and what it is used for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le05ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le05ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Sally's Suitcase </span></p>Where is the Middle East? It's an area in Western Asia and Egypt. Some people think it's an endless desert of rolling dunes with nomads riding on camels. Well, that's all in the past. There's still a lot of sand but today most people travel in cars and trucks."}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "24500", "text": "Camels were once the way to travel through the desert. They were used for transport, shade, milk, and meat. The nomads constantly moved their tents, families, and animals from one place to another. Their camels carried everything."}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "41500", "text": "Today, many people here live in urban and rural areas. You don't see many camels in a city or village. The tribes of wandering people wearing colorful, unique clothing are gone. Instead, people here live and dress as people do everywhere."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le05ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can talk about geographic features.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say where places are in a country. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about general quantities using words like more or less.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Would you take a ride on a camel?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What about an elephant or a horse? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2